    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0481" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg411"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>M . F. W. Seward to Mr.
                        Campbell</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 5, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On inquiry it is found that both the vessels you mention are employed in other
                    duty, from which they cannot be spared; and the Navy Department has none in your
                    vicinity that is available. You will therefore proceed by whatever conveyance or
                    route you may find most speedy or practicable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis D. Campbell,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">New Orleans.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
